[
    {
        "content": "<p>Currently we have two ways of talking about the conjugation action in group theory: <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=ConjAct#doc\">docs#ConjAct</a> (a type synonym) and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=MulAut.conj#doc\">docs#MulAut.conj</a> (the homomorphism)</p>\n<p>This has led to a bit of inconsistency in the library where some results are stated in terms of one or the other or both. Should we be preferring one over the other?</p>\n<p>I'm personally partial to <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=MulAut.conj#doc\">docs#MulAut.conj</a> since it retains the action (<code>MulAut.conj g • h</code> vs <code>ConjAct.toConjAct g • h</code>) while allowing one to talk about the actual automorphism in question (<code>MulAut.conj g</code>). <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=MulAut.conj#doc\">docs#MulAut.conj</a> has also been nicely to_additivized recently. But I'd be curious to hear other people's thoughts.</p>",
        "id": 624553417,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Browning",
        "timestamp": 1789542983
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(if we end up preferring <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=MulAut.conj#doc\">docs#MulAut.conj</a>, then there's also the follow-up question of whether we should prefer <code>MulAut.conj g • H</code> vs <code>H.map (MulAut.conj g)</code>).</p>",
        "id": 624554097,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Browning",
        "timestamp": 1789543164
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't regard the <code>to_additive</code> argument as persuasive,  since conjugation is only interesting in non-commutative groups, and it's very unusual to write non-commutative groups in additive notation.</p>",
        "id": 624554639,
        "sender_full_name": "David Loeffler",
        "timestamp": 1789543319
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>FWIW, this discussion arose out of reviwing modular-forms PR's where <code>ConjAct</code> is used, but that's largely arbitrary, I think I didn't know <code>MulAut.conj</code> existed when the code was first written.</p>",
        "id": 624555344,
        "sender_full_name": "David Loeffler",
        "timestamp": 1789543471
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It seems that <code>ConjAct</code> is not additivized at all? (and neither is <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=MulAut.conjNormal#doc\">docs#MulAut.conjNormal</a> btw)</p>",
        "id": 624558372,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1789544159
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"481963\">David Loeffler</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/ConjAct.20vs.20MulAut.2Econj/near/624554639\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I don't regard the <code>to_additive</code> argument as persuasive,  since conjugation is only interesting in non-commutative groups, and it's very unusual to write non-commutative groups in additive notation.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>If I recall correctly, I think non-additivization of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=MulAut.conj#doc\">docs#MulAut.conj</a> was blocking the construction of the profinite completion of the integers: <a class=\"message-link\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Profinite.20integers/near/577355977\">#mathlib4 &gt; Profinite integers @ 💬</a> </p>\n<p>So somehow this sort of mathematically absurd \"conjugation on additive structures\" has a habit of trickling down into sensible situations.</p>",
        "id": 624562620,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Browning",
        "timestamp": 1789545204
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Here is a reason that I prefer <code>MulAut.conj</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Group</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">MulAut</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">conj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"bp\">⁻¹</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"bp\">⁻¹</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- succeed</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Group</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">ConjAct</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toConjAct</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"bp\">⁻¹</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"bp\">⁻¹</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- fail because `(ConjAct.toConjAct g)⁻¹` is SNF. See `ConjAct.toConjAct_inv`</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 624567896,
        "sender_full_name": "Jiaxi Mo",
        "timestamp": 1789546279
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>One advantage of ConjAct is that you can talk about morphisms that preserve conjugation actions</p>",
        "id": 624574354,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1789547785
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"1097608\">Jiaxi Mo</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/ConjAct.20vs.20MulAut.2Econj/near/624567896\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Here is a reason that I prefer <code>MulAut.conj</code>:</p>\n<p><div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Group</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">MulAut</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">conj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"bp\">⁻¹</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"bp\">⁻¹</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- succeed</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Group</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">ConjAct</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toConjAct</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"bp\">⁻¹</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"bp\">⁻¹</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- fail because `(ConjAct.toConjAct g)⁻¹` is SNF. See `ConjAct.toConjAct_inv`</span>\n</code></pre></div><br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I think this isn't an intrinsic design advantage of <code>MulAut</code> over <code>ConjAct</code>, but rather a weakness in the <code>ConjAct</code> implementation – <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Algebra/Group/End.html#MulAut.conj_apply\"><code>MulAut.conj_apply</code></a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Algebra/Group/End.html#MulAut.conj_symm_apply\"><code>MulAut.conj_symm_apply</code></a> are simp lemmas, while their ConjAct analogues are not, and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/GroupTheory/GroupAction/ConjAct.html#ConjAct.toConjAct_inv_smul\"><code>ConjAct.toConjAct_inv_smul</code></a> is not in simp-normal form. </p>\n<p>I guess this raises the question of whether we should fix these API deficiencies in <code>ConjAct</code> to make the second example work, or discourage use of ConjAct to save the trouble of fixing it.</p>",
        "id": 624584999,
        "sender_full_name": "David Loeffler",
        "timestamp": 1789550221
    },
